# Provider model options (extendParams / option menus)

Custom “model extension” toggles (gear icon → popover) **must stay aligned with what each vendor’s HTTP API actually accepts.** Wrong or invented parameters cause empty responses, rejected requests, or broken tool calling.

## Authority order

1. **Official vendor documentation** — API reference, OpenAPI/schema, changelog, model tables (“only model `X` accepts field `Y`”).
2. **Structured schema** — e.g. Moonshot chat request `components/schemas/KimiK26ChatRequest` on [platform.moonshot.cn docs](https://platform.moonshot.cn/docs/api/chat).
3. **Secondary research** — Context7 / MCP docs fetch **only when** grounded in vendor docs; resolve conflicts in favor of the vendor.

Do **not** expose a toggle because another provider has a similarly named feature. Do **not** invent request-body keys (e.g. Minimax/OpenAI-compat flags) without documentation.

## End-to-end mapping (every new option)

Each real capability should be traced through **all** of these unless intentionally UI-only:

| Layer | Location (typical) |
|-------|-------------------|
| Catalogue | `packages/model-bank/src/aiModels/<provider>.ts` — `settings.extendParams?: ExtendParamsType[]` per **model id** |
| ExtendParams union | `packages/model-bank/src/types/aiModel.ts` — add a new union member only when wiring is real |
| Agent config | `packages/types/src/agent/chatConfig.ts` — field + `AgentChatConfigSchema` when persisted |
| Request assembly | `src/services/chat/index.ts` — map `chatConfig` → `ChatStreamPayload` / `extendParams` |
| Provider runtime | `packages/model-runtime/src/providers/<provider>/` — exact JSON body; unit tests for payload shape |
| UI | Provider-specific panel (see below) + i18n (`src/locales/default/chat.ts` + `locales/en-US|zh-CN/chat.json`) |

If the doc says a field applies **only** to certain model IDs, gate **`extendParams` on those cards** and gate runtime branches on `payload.model` — do not send the field for other ids.

## UI pattern: one provider panel at a time

- **Dispatcher:** e.g. `src/features/ChatInput/ActionBar/Model/index.tsx` — `provider === 'moonshot'` → `<MoonshotOptions />`, else `<ControlsForm />` until that provider is migrated.
- **Provider component:** e.g. `.../Model/providers/MoonshotOptions.tsx` — build `Form` items from `aiModelSelectors.modelExtendParams(model, provider)` only; compact popover width / responsive desc copy as needed.
- **Migration strategy:** ship **one provider per iteration**; keep `ControlsForm` as default for unmigrated providers. Avoid dumping every vendor into one monolithic form with misleading shared copy (e.g. Claude-only reasoning text on Kimi).

Gear visibility remains **`isModelHasExtendParams`** — empty `extendParams` means no gear.

## Testing and regression

- Add or extend **runtime unit tests** on `build*Payload` / `handlePayload` when behavior is non-trivial (thinking toggles, tool + thinking interaction, optional fields like `thinking.keep`).
- After changes, run **`bash scripts/type-check-tsc.sh`** and targeted **`bun test`** for touched packages.

## Shipping

Follow **`.cursor/rules/git-and-release.mdc`** — **no commit / tag / push without an explicit in-turn user instruction** unless the user asked to ship.

## Quick checklist (new module or new toggle)

- [ ] Confirmed in **official** API docs / schema for **this** model id.
- [ ] `extendParams` updated on the right model card(s); union type extended if new key.
- [ ] `chatConfig` + Zod if persisted; service mapping updated.
- [ ] Provider runtime sends **only** documented fields; tests updated.
- [ ] Provider option panel + i18n; no shared Anthropic-specific copy on other vendors.
